{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡8x{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-10049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/ja