d}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114687" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-114687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "4-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "4x+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "4x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] ["math" "4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114687" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡8x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/020a73150209de3ee6f95fa1b21c85bd5673e500e4e421459eff90d2dd1a42e9.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+2x+1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2}).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{2})+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+(\\pi )^{2}+\\pi ]-[3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+(0)^{2}+0] \\\\  & =[0+{\\pi }^{2}+\\pi ]-0 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}+\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-348731" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348731" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi^2+\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{sin}^{2}⁡x+7{cos}^{2}⁡x & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x+3{cos}^{2}⁡x+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+4{cos}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(3+4{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[3+\\frac{4}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(5+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(5x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[5\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})]-[5\\cdot 0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})]-[0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+1]-[0+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi +4}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-361705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)+x-1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348766" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi^2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {cos}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡3x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{1}{2}x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-74787" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74787" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74787" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{x}{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression $4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2.\n$$\n\nThus, the integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(4{cos}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-348737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 4{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =2x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-114691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x))={sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-347169" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74410" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-74410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-74410" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/24f2892d622c6a28eb5f95a89f0e1ae7223b07e6219f50698ecef3d0c1c08e1a.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve\n$y=2x-{sin}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{2},$\nthe $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=2x-{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2},$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x-{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x-{sin}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}))-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{16}-\\frac{1}{4})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-348876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348876" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi^2}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})-1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-114712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-114712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}[4{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{6})-2+4cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})]\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6}$, we have\n\n$$\n4{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{6})=2(1-cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,\\,[4{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{6})-2+4cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})]dx & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\,\\,[2-2cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})-2+4cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}2cos\\,(\\frac{x}{3})\\,dx \\\\  & =6sin\\,(\\frac{x}{3}){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =6[sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{6})] \\\\  & =6(1-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348884" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4630758fe7518876b4078da53f63d140afc115ff54e30376f6c8b26fc3d8c081"} {"question" "q-348884" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "q-348884" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/state.json" "file_sha256" "f0cb13d088b022db56deb1f0839d4c465912f56d5e2acf5c345df70dcd9ae9bb"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db"} {"question" "e-481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}.\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x\t&= \\sin \\left( \\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos  \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right).\n  }\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left( - \\cos {x}\\right )+C \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-481.json" "file_sha256" "575d6659f0b7588e18f585207fdfd5ea75ce6bb10647cdc8212f640b33f7d3db"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766"} {"question" "e-484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-484.json" "file_sha256" "66ec5d5bb9092490b8f02f7d219d78ac40dd2bc4e9e8d04cbea1369808e4f766"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866"} {"question" "e-482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int ( \\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x\\[5pt]\n                                                                 &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-482.json" "file_sha256" "b7d050412a399bfb55d35047555b4be04f2ddcd8ec9d9c3b85ffccc9ae7c5866"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab"} {"question" "e-483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right )=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right )=\\sin^2(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/example-483.json" "file_sha256" "d4589f3407741b43cf9c39629536db1e81b0616e2a68d55c923258253899d4ab"}] "usage" {"q-10423" [] "e-484" [] "e-481" [] "e-482" [] "e-483" []} "basis" 1133 "retractions" [[17592186096849 :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$∫(\\sin x\\cos x - 5)dx$."] [17592186096394 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{{\\int}} \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096394 :question/worked-solution "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta} =2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin(2\\theta) = \\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}\n$$\n\nLetting\n\n$$\n\\theta= \\dfrac{x}{2}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin \\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{x}{2} \\right) &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2} \\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin x &= \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right). \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int \\sin \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin {x} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(-\\cos {x}\\right)+C \\\\[5pt] &=-\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cos {x}+C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096397 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096397 :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} {\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\ &=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096395 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096395 :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\cos^2{x}$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1\n$$\n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right)\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int \\cos^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cos 2x +1 \\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\int (\\cos {2x} +1) \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sin {2x} +x\\right) + C \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sin {2x} +\\dfrac{1}{2}x + C. \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096396 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin^2(3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096396 :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the $\\sin^2$ term:\n\n$$\n\\cos {2\\theta}=1-2\\sin^2\\theta\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {2\\theta} \\right)=\\sin^2\\theta\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos {6x} \\right)=\\sin^2(3x)\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\sin^{2} (3x)dx &= ∫\\frac{1}{2}(1 - \\cos 6x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(1 - \\cos 6x)dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(x - \\frac{1}{6}\\sin 6x) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}x - \\frac{1}{12}\\sin 6x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186093502 17592186093503 17592186093504 17592186093505 17592186093506] "immutable_fields" [[17592186093501 :answer-field/correct] [17592186093501 :answer-field/id] [17592186093501 :answer-field/key] [17592186093501 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
